  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "The construction technique of this type of reinforced brick masonry consists of placing steel reinforcement bars at the junction of the brick courses. The behavior of the reinforced brick layer is similar to that of a reinforced concrete beam. The thin-shell, single-thickness brick structure derives its rigidity and strength from a double-curved catenary arch form that resists buckling failure."
